
node_modules/
dist/
# EVERY .env, then the two that are deliberately tracked. This used to name the
# variants one at a time — .env, .env.local, .env.*.local, .env.miner — which
# covers the files people actually create and misses the ones Vite ALSO loads:
# a plain .env.production or .env.development would have been committed. On a
# PUBLIC repo whose build inlines every VITE_ prefixed value into a public
# bundle, that is the same hazard scripts/key-exposure-smoke.mjs exists for,
# arriving one step earlier — before the build, in the diff.
#
# Deny-by-default with two exceptions is the shape that cannot be incomplete:
# a new .env variant is ignored the day someone invents it, and adding a
# deliberately-tracked one is an edit here rather than an omission.
.env*
!.env.preview
!.env.miner.example

# Scratch harness for rendering sheets at 390pt during design work.
.preview/
.preview-dist/
